Chapter: ProbeClosureContagion

 The sharpest form of the question. `relay-once` is DEFINED and never
 called. The driver exercises only `make-adder`, which prints 47 both in
 probe-closure-solo.codex and in probe-closure-return.codex.

 `contagion 47` means a bad definition only hurts callers of itself.
 A fault means merely DEFINING a function is enough to miscompile a
 different, correct function in the same chapter -- damage that no
 reading of the working definition could predict, and that arrives
 without the bad definition ever running.

Section: Shapes

  add3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add3 (x) (y) (z) = x + y + z

  make-adder : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  make-adder (n) = add3 n

 Defined, never called.

  relay-once : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  relay-once (n) = make-adder n

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("contagion " & show (((make-adder 5) 20) 22))
  end
